# Line endings are pinned, not left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# This repository is installed by running shell scripts on Linux. A CRLF shebang
# fails with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", which is an instant, total,
# and confusing failure on a contributor's Raspberry Pi — and the contributor is
# the person least equipped to diagnose it. The systemd unit and the config
# example have the same problem in a quieter form.
#
# eol=lf applies to the working copy as well as the blob, so a checkout on a
# Windows workstation still produces files that run correctly under WSL.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly LF, since these are the ones that break loudly.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.go      text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.example text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.gz  binary
*.pem binary
